{
    "background_story": "Maxwell was a mystic who had spent his life studying the ancient arts of energy manipulation. He believed that the true nature of reality was formless, a boundless expanse of pure energy waiting to be shaped by the human mind. Through years of meditation and practice, Maxwell had learned to tap into this energy, allowing him to transcend the limitations of the physical world. He could dissolve his molecular structure at will, becoming one with the air and the ether. Maxwell's formless state allowed him to move through solid objects, traverse vast distances in an instant, and even communicate with other beings on a spiritual level. His existence was a testament to the idea that the only true constant is change, and that the boundaries of reality are but a mere illusion.",
